WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.593
Columbus took Mandy to his cabin.

2
00:00:03.594 --> 00:00:07.259
"You will be safe here," he said.

3
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:11.896
Curious, Mandy picked up a round metal object.

4
00:00:11.897 --> 00:00:16.372
Its pointy, moving hands were like a clock’s.

5
00:00:16.373 --> 00:00:20.307
"What’s this?" asked Mandy.

6
00:00:20.308 --> 00:00:24.179
"It’s an astrolabe," explained Columbus.

7
00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:27.647
"It measures the height of the sun from the horizon.

8
00:00:27.648 --> 00:00:31.328
It helps us know where we are on the ocean."

9
00:00:31.329 --> 00:00:34.595
Columbus took the astrolabe and said,

10
00:00:34.596 --> 00:00:40.022
"I have to go now. Stay here."

11
00:00:40.023 --> 00:00:43.730
Meanwhile, Vinnie was getting hungry.

12
00:00:43.731 --> 00:00:47.381
A sailor’s life wasn’t much fun.

13
00:00:47.382 --> 00:00:52.609
"We’re all going to starve," said an old sailor nearby.

14
00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:58.139
"Monsters will eat us before we starve!" screamed another.

15
00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:02.210
"I want to go home!" thought Vinnie.

16
00:01:02.211 --> 00:01:05.805
Manuel was tying a knot in a rope.

17
00:01:05.806 --> 00:01:12.196
Another boy was standing by a large coil of rope, holding an hourglass.

18
00:01:12.197 --> 00:01:16.627
When the sand emptied into the bottom, the boy cried:

19
00:01:16.628 --> 00:01:18.756
"One glass is gone.

20
00:01:18.757 --> 00:01:21.118
Now the second begins!"

21
00:01:21.119 --> 00:01:25.141
"What’s he doing?" Vinnie asked Manuel.

22
00:01:25.142 --> 00:01:28.539
"We take turns turning over the hourglass.

23
00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:34.366
Each time it empties, a half hour has gone by," explained Manuel.

24
00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:39.843
"After eight turns, or four hours, another boy takes over."

25
00:01:39.844 --> 00:01:42.140
The boy called to Vinnie,

26
00:01:42.141 --> 00:01:44.759
"Hey, take over a minute, will you?"

27
00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:48.341
He put the hourglass into Vinnie’s hands.

28
00:01:48.342 --> 00:01:52.444
"It’s the second half of the hour," said the boy.

29
00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:56.215
He ran off before Vinnie could protest.

30
00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:58.885
"Here," said Manuel.

31
00:01:58.886 --> 00:02:03.351
He took a biscuit out of his pocket and gave it to Vinnie.

32
00:02:03.352 --> 00:02:09.093
Biscuits were used to mark the time after each turn of the hourglass. Vinnie

33
00:02:09.094 --> 00:02:12.610
thought he was supposed to eat it. "Ow!"

34
00:02:12.611 --> 00:02:16.817
cried Vinnie, after he tried to bite it. The

35
00:02:16.818 --> 00:02:21.814
biscuit was so hard that Vinnie put it down on the ropes. Meanwhile,

36
00:02:21.815 --> 00:02:26.437
Mandy sat alone in the captain’s cabin. The

37
00:02:26.438 --> 00:02:30.356
cabin boy had left her a biscuit to eat. She

38
00:02:30.357 --> 00:02:32.722
put it in her pocket. Suddenly,

39
00:02:32.723 --> 00:02:36.592
there was a loud boom. Mandy,

40
00:02:36.593 --> 00:02:40.076
ran out onto the deck. "What

41
00:02:40.077 --> 00:02:43.790
was that?" she shouted. "It’s

42
00:02:43.791 --> 00:02:47.310
the Pinta! " cried someone.

43
00:02:47.311 --> 00:02:49.618
"The ship needs help!"

44
00:02:49.619 --> 00:02:54.159
At that moment, she heard a familiar voice shouting,

45
00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:58.855
"One glass is gone, and now the second begins!"

46
00:02:58.856 --> 00:03:02.656
"Vinnie!" she cried happily.

47
00:03:02.657 --> 00:03:06.284
"Mandy! Am I glad to see you!"

48
00:03:06.285 --> 00:03:09.106
he exclaimed when she ran up.

49
00:03:09.107 --> 00:03:12.882
He put the hourglass on top of the ropes.

50
00:03:12.883 --> 00:03:16.641
"What are you doing?" she asked.

51
00:03:16.642 --> 00:03:21.637
"Every thirty minutes, I turn this hourglass over.

52
00:03:21.638 --> 00:03:25.875
Each time, Manuel brings a biscuit.

53
00:03:25.876 --> 00:03:30.336
They’re so hard I can’t eat them," said Vinnie.

54
00:03:30.337 --> 00:03:32.262
"Don’t eat them!"

55
00:03:32.263 --> 00:03:36.131
Mandy shouted, pulling out the photo.

56
00:03:36.132 --> 00:03:39.437
"We need them! See?"

57
00:03:39.438 --> 00:03:42.218
The photo was glowing blue.

58
00:03:42.219 --> 00:03:46.853
"But there are only two biscuits!" cried Vinnie.

59
00:03:46.854 --> 00:03:49.539
"We need three to go home."

60
00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:55.763
"Don’t worry," said Mandy, pulling the biscuit from her pocket.

61
00:03:55.764 --> 00:03:59.874
Mandy placed it next to the other biscuits.

62
00:03:59.875 --> 00:04:04.492
In the photo, the hourglass glowed red.

63
00:04:04.493 --> 00:04:09.003
"I’m so glad we’re leaving!" cried Vinnie.

64
00:04:09.004 --> 00:04:17.324
The children closed their eyes and fell down the dark tunnel.

